  "summary": "Jadeite is presumed one of the most precious materials of Pre-Columbian Costa Rica.",
  "description": "Jadeite is presumed one of the most precious materials of Pre-Columbian Costa Rica.  It, along with other similar-looking greenstones (e.g. chalcedony, serpentine, and green jasper) were cherished and worked for years.  Jadeite was used to decorate the body and was presumably a symbol of power.",
